jobs.prompt:
You are job t101-vendor. Restate done-when in one line. Vendor five MIT worker skills from the upstream copies in your context (files named <skill>.SKILL.md plus reference files <skill>.<ref>.md, and LICENSE) into templates/coordination/skills/<name>/ for name in: tdd, diagnosing-bugs, code-review, resolving-merge-conflicts, writing-for-agents.
Per skill write: SKILL.md = our frontmatter (name, description one line, paths: list, checks: with resultKeys list; copy the exact frontmatter style and parser limits of the two example skills named oasis-*.SKILL.md in context, and tools/skills.mjs) + the upstream body trimmed to the rules a bounded file-tools worker can act on (drop install steps, interactive/human-in-the-loop steps, shell-script references, slash-command and plugin talk, links to files we do not ship). Whole file <= 800 tokens (ceil(chars/4) <= 800, i.e. <= 3200 chars); keep the upstream's meaning and wording where kept. A trimmed-away part that matters may go in one reference file beside it (tdd: tests.md/mocking.md trimmed, writing-for-agents: mechanics) each <= 3200 chars. LICENSE = the upstream MIT LICENSE text verbatim in every skill folder. Add a first body line: 'Adapted from mattpocock/skills (MIT), commit <pin>; trimmed.' Pins: 6fd947921b935b7e1e69293a200400f0fdd5c15f for tdd, diagnosing-bugs, code-review, writing-for-agents; 153fc1b93de6584562765cdce299324e1ff9e661 for resolving-merge-conflicts (removed upstream later; last version). paths: choose generic globs (e.g. tests/** and src/** for tdd; no project names).
Also: append a 'Third-party worker skills' section to NOTICE (repo, license, both pins, list of skills, 'trimmed and adapted'). Make tools/install.mjs copy each templates/coordination/skills/<name>/ folder (every file in it) to coordination/skills/<name>/ only when that folder is absent (never overwrite or merge an existing project skill of the same name), reported in the existing added/kept lists. Tests in tests/t101-vendored-skills.test.mjs: each of the five loads with the tools/skills.mjs loader without error and estimates <= 800 tokens (no skill-over-800 warning); each folder has LICENSE identical to the upstream MIT text and a pin line; NOTICE names both pins; install copies the folders into a fresh fixture root and keeps an existing coordination/skills/code-review untouched (byte-identical). No new dependencies. Private names: no person, company, product or repo names other than the upstream attribution. CHANGELOG.md and version files are owned by another job; do not edit or block on them. Do not run the full suite (nested sandbox reds are expected); you may run node --test tests/t101-vendored-skills.test.mjs tests/install.test.mjs tests/worker-skills.test.mjs. Return JSON only: {"status":"complete|blocked","filesChanged":[...],"reproTest":"tests/t101-vendored-skills.test.mjs","notes":"<=3 lines: final token estimate per skill"}
